6},"status":"FINISHED","studios":[{"animation":false,"id":109,"name":"Shouchiku"},{"animation":true,"id":7805,"name":"Cypic"},{"animation":false,"id":7232,"name":"CyberAgent"},{"animation":false,"id":6310,"name":"Cygames"},{"animation":false,"id":6715,"name":"Toy's Factory"},{"animation":false,"id":7161,"name":"arma bianca"},{"animation":false,"id":6259,"name":"TOKYO MX"},{"animation":false,"id":6796,"name":"BS Asahi"},{"animation":false,"id":7313,"name":"Happinet Media Marketing"}],"synopsis":{"language":null,"source":"anilist","spoiler":false,"text":"Born into a life of acting and dance with a traveling theater troupe in 14th-century Japan, 12-year old Oniyasha has one problem—he doesn't know what the point of any of it is. \"Why must I step with the left foot here instead of the right? Why is one performance good and another, bad? Why do people dance at all?\" It all seems perfectly arbitrary, until a chance encounter in a run-down shack sets him down a path to revolutionizing the art form and influencing much of Japanese culture to come. A fictionalized account of the early life of Zeami Motokiyo (Oniyasha), the founder of modern Noh theater—the world's oldest surviving theater art—this coming-of-age artist's journey vividly brings to life a man far ahead of his time during one of Japan's most culturally and socially vibrant eras.\n\n(Source: Kodansha Comics)\n\nNote: World Is Dancing streamed 3 days in advance of the TV broadcast on Prime Video and HIDIVE beginning June 29th, 2026. Regular broadcasting began on July 2nd, 2026."},"tags":[{"name":"Historical","rank":97,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dancing","rank":94,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Coming of Age","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Musical Theater","rank":72,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Class Struggle","rank":72,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Acting","rank":68,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Biographical","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Crossdressing","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":56,"s